Subject: [PATCH] fix(convo): path.head keeps the conversation in its ancestry

derive_path took the last emitted step as path.head, which is the last
event step. A Claude Code session's attachment events are parented to
the first user turn, so they formed a side chain off it and the head
landed at its tip: every assistant turn sat outside ancestors(head), so
by the format's rule the conversation itself was a dead end (drawn that
way in toolpath.net's visualizer). pick_head takes the latest step whose
ancestry holds the last turn. The claude and claude-session goldens now
head at claude-preamble-8; no other set has an event side chain. pr/34.
